A C# message bus defines a handler interface whose type parameter appears only as a method parameter:

```csharp
interface IHandler<T>
{
    void Handle(T message);
}
```

A team has a logging handler that implements `IHandler<object>`. They want to assign it to a variable of type `IHandler<string>` without casts or wrapper classes. Fill in the variance keyword that makes this assignment compile:

`interface IHandler<{{marking}} T>`
